# Line endings: the repository is LF, and the working tree is kept LF too.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` checks text files out
# with CRLF. gofmt / goimports then treat every line as modified, so `make lint`
# and `make fmt-check` fail locally while CI (Linux, LF) stays green.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary per file (binaries are left alone);
# `eol=lf` pins the checkout form so the result is the same on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must never be CRLF: a CRLF shebang line, or a CRLF after a `\`
# line continuation, breaks bash on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf
